content.text:
# PR Discussion History

_Previous review discussions for PR #1164._

> ℹ️ **1 machine notice(s) excluded (arming/status boilerplate — never reply targets).**

## Review Threads (Inline Comments)

### Thread 1 — `createQuestionsAndAssignForReview.js` line 132

**dmtools-factory-bot** (2026-10-22):
⚠️ **IMPORTANT: `ai_questions_asked` label is hardcoded — bypasses the configurable `labels.AI_QUESTIONS_ASKED`**

This action already resolves `projectConfig.labels.QUESTION` for the question-subtask label (line 57), but the parent label is a string literal:

```javascript
tracker.addLabel(ticketKey, 'ai_questions_asked');
```

The parity target, `js/createQuestionsAndAssignForReview.js`, uses the project config instead:

```javascript
getTracker().addLabel(ticketKey, labels.AI_QUESTIONS_ASKED);
```

(`AI_QUESTIONS_ASKED: 'ai_questions_asked'` is the default in `js/config.js:54` — projects can override it via `.dmtools/config.js`.) A deployment that overrides this label gets the default from the legacy root script and the override from the packed one — two copies of the same workflow disagreeing.

Suggested fix:

```javascript
var labels = (projectConfig && projectConfig.labels) || {};
tracker.addLabel(ticketKey, labels.AI_QUESTIONS_ASKED || 'ai_questions_asked');
```

---

### Thread 2 — `createQuestionsAndAssignForReview.js` line 37

**dmtools-factory-bot** (2026-10-22):
⚠️ **IMPORTANT: ADO question subtasks get the question label, Jira ones do not**

The new ADO path labels each created question:

```javascript
// createAdoQuestionTicket (line 57)
var result = tracker.createTicketWithParent(projectKey, adoType, summary, description, parentKey, {
    labels: [questionLabel]
});
```

…but the Jira path (`buildJiraQuestionFields`, this hunk) builds `fieldsJson` with `summary`/`description`/`issuetype`/`parent`/`priority` and **no `labels` field**, so question subtasks created on Jira carry no question label. The canonical `js/createQuestionsAndAssignForReview.js` includes `labels: [questionLabel]` in the Jira `fieldsJson` as well — so the two copies of the workflow disagree, and any downstream filtering of question subtasks by label behaves differently per provider (the label is genuinely used by the new ADO branch, so the Jira omission is now visible).

Old root behavior is preserved for Jira (legacy code also sent no labels), so this is not a regression — but since the PR routes both providers through one abstraction, aligning the Jira branch with the js/ script removes the asymmetry:

```javascript
function buildJiraQuestionFields(summary, description, parentKey, priority, questionLabel) {
    var fieldsJson = {
        summary: summary,
        description: description,
        issuetype: { name: 'Subtask' },
        parent: { key: parentKey },
        labels: [questionLabel]
    };
    ...
}
```

---

### Thread 3 — `assignForReview.js` line 59

**dmtools-factory-bot** (2026-10-22):
⚠️ **IMPORTANT: Undocumented behavior change — WIP-label removal and `targetStatus` in the legacy root script**

The PR description for this file says: *"Resolve projectConfig and customParams, instantiate tracker via trackers.createTracker, forward tracker/config/customParams into tokenUsageComment.postTokenUsageComments, and pass tracker to jiraHelpers.assignForReview"* — but the diff also adds two behavior changes:

1. `resolveWipLabel` (line 25) + passing `wipLabel` — after hand-off the `<contextId>_wip` label is now **removed** from the ticket. Previously the legacy root script left it in place.
2. `params.targetStatus` (line 52) — the hand-off status is now caller-selectable instead of always "In Review".

Both mirror `js/assignForReview.js` parity (which builds the same WIP label and passes `STATUSES.SOLUTION_ARCHITECTURE`), the removal is graceful (a missing label only warns inside `trackers.assignForReview`), and this repo's SM rules support `targetStatus` — so the change looks intentional and safe.

